    "note": "Annual MIN-MAX per station as CPCB prints it; no midpoint is derived. CPCB's 2019-2024 tables list no river station in Visakhapatnam: these are the reservoir, creek and canal stations on the three channels. Station 5678 is attached to the Meghadri Gedda by measured distance to the OSM line (geometry_check).",
    "conventions": {
      "reading_shape": "{min, max} for the calendar year, as published. Blank, '-' and BDL cells are null.",
      "nitrogen": "CPCB's nitrogen column is nitrogen as N (NO3-N + NO2-N in most editions, NO3-N alone in 2023 and the 2024 split files; nitrogen_basis per reading). It is not nitrate as NO3, so nitrate_mgl is null and nothing here is compared with the 45 mg/L BIS nitrate limit.",
      "typed_single_value_fields": "conductivity_us, cod_mgl and tds_mgl are typed as single numbers and the shared panel renders them so; CPCB prints ranges, carried as conductivity_us_range, cod_mgl_range and tds_mgl_range.",
      "split_2024": "2024 values come from the combined annual table where CPCB published one (4356, 5678), with samples, BOD mean, COD and TDS from the split files. 5160 and 4927 appear only in the split files. The one disagreement: 5678 pH minimum is 6.1 in the combined creek table and 6.05 in the split file; 6.1 is used.",
